From: Florian Maurer <fmaurer@disroot.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:49:11 +0000
Subject: mac80211: ath11k: fix firmware crash recovery on AHB

Add the patches posted to linux-wireless for the remaining recovery
problems on IPQ8074, which are not merged yet:

- 455-459: "wifi: ath11k: firmware crash recovery fixes" v2 by Julius
  Bairaktaris. A failed recovery no longer frees the radios or the srng
  allocations, TX stays blocked until the rings are set up again, and
  only the restart work sends WMI commands during a recovery.
- 460, 461: "wifi: ath11k: more firmware crash recovery fixes for AHB".
  The ext IRQs are not disabled twice after a failed recovery, and TX is
  stopped from the remoteproc SSR notifier before WCSS is reset.

"wifi: ath11k: depend on RPMSG instead of selecting it" of the second
series is left out. It only avoids a recursive Kconfig dependency with
461, and the select of RPMSG it replaces (32ec8488d75d) is not in
backports-6.18.55.

Not covered: a second firmware crash 10-20 ms after the firmware is up
again can make the next recovery dereference the cleared srngs in
ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes().

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/20261018210153.1925962-1-julius@bairaktaris.de/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/cover.1793531790.git.fmaurer@disroot.org/
Assisted-by: LLM

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/455-wifi-ath11k-initialise-the-CE-descriptor-waitqueue-once-per-device.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/455-wifi-ath11k-initialise-the-CE-descriptor-waitqueue-once-per-device.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d3612e4e5a49121ead0cd636f29e4cc41fbaf817
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/455-wifi-ath11k-initialise-the-CE-descriptor-waitqueue-once-per-device.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:01:49 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: initialise the CE descriptor waitqueue once per device
+
+Firmware crash recovery reinitialises tx_ce_desc_wq in
+ath11k_connect_pdev_htc_service(), reached through ath11k_core_start()
+and ath11k_wmi_connect(), while a WMI command on a device without credit
+flow can still sleep on it in ath11k_wmi_cmd_send(). finish_wait() then
+unlinks the waiter from the reset list head:
+
+  list_del corruption. prev->next should be ffffffc084293648, but was
+  ffffff80075109a8. (prev=ffffff80075109a8)
+  WARNING: CPU: 2 PID: 1782 at lib/list_debug.c:62
+  __list_del_entry_valid_or_report+0x134/0x174
+  CPU: 2 UID: 101 PID: 1782 Comm: hostapd
+  Call trace:
+   __list_del_entry_valid_or_report+0x134/0x174 (P)
+   finish_wait+0x68/0xb8
+   ath11k_wmi_cmd_send+0x150/0x2f4 [ath11k]
+   ath11k_wmi_vdev_set_param_cmd+0x64/0xd8 [ath11k]
+   ath11k_mac_op_bss_info_changed+0xe8/0xf6c [ath11k]
+   drv_link_info_changed+0x128/0x180 [mac80211]
+   ieee80211_link_info_change_notify+0xe0/0x100 [mac80211]
+   ieee80211_change_bss+0x1bc/0x250 [mac80211]
+   nl80211_set_bss+0x1a0/0x328 [cfg80211]
+
+Initialise the queues once in ath11k_core_alloc().
+
+Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1
+
+Fixes: f951380a6022 ("ath11k: Disabling credit flow for WMI path")
+Reviewed-by: Baochen Qiang <baochen.qiang@oss.qualcomm.com>
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+@@ -2713,6 +2713,7 @@ struct ath11k_base *ath11k_core_alloc(struct device *dev, size_t priv_size,
+ 				      enum ath11k_bus bus)
+ {
+ 	struct ath11k_base *ab;
++	int i;
+ 
+ 	ab = kzalloc(sizeof(*ab) + priv_size, GFP_KERNEL);
+ 	if (!ab)
+@@ -2739,6 +2740,10 @@ struct ath11k_base *ath11k_core_alloc(struct device *dev, size_t priv_size,
+ 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&ab->peers);
+ 	init_waitqueue_head(&ab->peer_mapping_wq);
+ 	init_waitqueue_head(&ab->wmi_ab.tx_credits_wq);
++
++	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ab->wmi_ab.wmi); i++)
++		init_waitqueue_head(&ab->wmi_ab.wmi[i].tx_ce_desc_wq);
++
+ 	init_waitqueue_head(&ab->qmi.cold_boot_waitq);
+ 	INIT_WORK(&ab->restart_work, ath11k_core_restart);
+ 	INIT_WORK(&ab->update_11d_work, ath11k_update_11d);
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+@@ -8945,7 +8945,6 @@ static int ath11k_connect_pdev_htc_service(struct ath11k_base *ab,
+ 	ab->wmi_ab.wmi_endpoint_id[pdev_idx] = conn_resp.eid;
+ 	ab->wmi_ab.wmi[pdev_idx].eid = conn_resp.eid;
+ 	ab->wmi_ab.max_msg_len[pdev_idx] = conn_resp.max_msg_len;
+-	init_waitqueue_head(&ab->wmi_ab.wmi[pdev_idx].tx_ce_desc_wq);
+ 
+ 	return 0;
+ }
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/456-wifi-ath11k-keep-the-radios-when-a-firmware-recovery-fails.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/456-wifi-ath11k-keep-the-radios-when-a-firmware-recovery-fails.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9c59741b5d8ffcab07c8b7d3fcd8fc3f70e75132
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/456-wifi-ath11k-keep-the-radios-when-a-firmware-recovery-fails.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:01:50 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: keep the radios when a firmware recovery fails
+
+On a firmware crash recovery ath11k_mac_allocate() keeps the registered
+radios, but the error paths of ath11k_core_start() and
+ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready() still call ath11k_mac_destroy(). A
+failed recovery thus frees an ieee80211_hw that mac80211 still uses and
+leaves ab->pdevs[i].ar NULL. A frame bridged to the radio then follows
+the freed hw:
+
+  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address
+  ffffff8316cfd480
+  pc : sta_info_hash_lookup+0x4c/0xe4 [mac80211]
+  Call trace:
+   sta_info_hash_lookup+0x4c/0xe4 [mac80211] (P)
+   sta_info_get_bss+0x1c/0x78 [mac80211]
+   ieee80211_lookup_ra_sta+0x124/0x14c [mac80211]
+   __ieee80211_subif_start_xmit+0xb8/0x3a0 [mac80211]
+   ieee80211_subif_start_xmit+0x50/0x750 [mac80211]
+   dev_hard_start_xmit+0x98/0x120
+
+and driver removal dereferences the NULL ar:
+
+  Unable to handle kernel access to user memory outside uaccess routines
+  at virtual address 0000000000000000
+  pc : ath11k_dp_rx_pdev_free+0x34/0x12c [ath11k]
+  Call trace:
+   ath11k_dp_rx_pdev_free+0x34/0x12c [ath11k] (P)
+   ath11k_dp_pdev_free+0x4c/0x84 [ath11k]
+   ath11k_core_deinit+0xdc/0x168 [ath11k]
+   ath11k_ahb_remove+0x30/0x90 [ath11k_ahb]
+
+Destroy the radios only when ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED is clear, as
+ath11k_mac_allocate() does.
+
+Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1
+
+Fixes: 0366f42640a4 ("ath11k: Move mac80211 hw allocation before wmi_init command")
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+@@ -2201,7 +2201,8 @@ static int ath11k_core_start(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ err_reo_cleanup:
+ 	ath11k_dp_pdev_reo_cleanup(ab);
+ err_mac_destroy:
+-	ath11k_mac_destroy(ab);
++	if (!test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags))
++		ath11k_mac_destroy(ab);
+ err_hif_stop:
+ 	ath11k_hif_stop(ab);
+ err_wmi_detach:
+@@ -2285,7 +2286,8 @@ int ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ 
+ err_core_stop:
+ 	ath11k_core_stop(ab);
+-	ath11k_mac_destroy(ab);
++	if (!test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags))
++		ath11k_mac_destroy(ab);
+ err_dp_free:
+ 	ath11k_dp_free(ab);
+ 	mutex_unlock(&ab->core_lock);
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/457-wifi-ath11k-keep-the-srng-allocations-when-a-firmware-recovery-fails.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/457-wifi-ath11k-keep-the-srng-allocations-when-a-firmware-recovery-fails.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cca8b1eb42641fa08b288e26f618c6e5c7c0e281
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/457-wifi-ath11k-keep-the-srng-allocations-when-a-firmware-recovery-fails.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:01:51 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: keep the srng allocations when a firmware recovery fails
+
+Since commit 32be3ca4cf78 ("wifi: ath11k: HAL SRNG: don't deinitialize
+and re-initialize again") recovery zeroes the hal state instead of
+freeing and reallocating it, but a failed recovery still calls
+ath11k_hal_srng_deinit(). This frees the ring pointer buffers and the
+ring configuration, which only probe allocates, while the rings still
+point into them. Driver removal then walks the copy engine rings through
+the freed buffers:
+
+  ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to reconfigure driver on crash recovery
+  ...
+  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address
+  ffffffc080ee5090
+  pc : ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc/0x60 [ath11k]
+  Call trace:
+   ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc/0x60 [ath11k] (P)
+   ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes+0x16c/0x4cc [ath11k]
+   ath11k_ahb_stop+0x2c/0x3c [ath11k_ahb]
+   ath11k_core_deinit+0xec/0x168 [ath11k]
+   ath11k_ahb_remove+0x30/0x90 [ath11k_ahb]
+
+Return the error and keep the allocations for ath11k_ahb_remove() and
+ath11k_pci_remove() to free.
+
+Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1
+
+Fixes: 32be3ca4cf78 ("wifi: ath11k: HAL SRNG: don't deinitialize and re-initialize again")
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+@@ -2321,15 +2321,11 @@ static int ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ 
+ 	ret = ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(ab);
+ 	if (ret)
+-		goto err_hal_srng_deinit;
++		return ret;
+ 
+ 	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags);
+ 
+ 	return 0;
+-
+-err_hal_srng_deinit:
+-	ath11k_hal_srng_deinit(ab);
+-	return ret;
+ }
+ 
+ void ath11k_core_halt(struct ath11k *ar)
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/458-wifi-ath11k-clear-CRASH_FLUSH-only-after-recovery-rebuilds-the-rings.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/458-wifi-ath11k-clear-CRASH_FLUSH-only-after-recovery-rebuilds-the-rings.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5f67bb629a09397f25edce2d70f59f18b0953f19
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/458-wifi-ath11k-clear-CRASH_FLUSH-only-after-recovery-rebuilds-the-rings.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:01:52 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: clear CRASH_FLUSH only after recovery rebuilds the rings
+
+ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() clears ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH right
+after ath11k_hal_srng_clear() zeroes the rings, but
+ath11k_ce_init_pipes() and ath11k_dp_alloc() rebuild them only later. A
+WMI command sent in between passes the CRASH_FLUSH check in
+ath11k_ce_send() and dereferences the NULL tail pointer of the cleared
+ring:
+
+  Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at virtual address 0
+  pc : ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc/0x60 [ath11k]
+  lr : ath11k_ce_send+0x114/0x350 [ath11k]
+  Call trace:
+   ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc/0x60 [ath11k] (P)
+   ath11k_htc_send+0x188/0x3c8 [ath11k]
+   ath11k_wmi_cmd_send+0xc8/0x2f4 [ath11k]
+   ath11k_wmi_send_peer_create_cmd+0x78/0xe0 [ath11k]
+   ath11k_peer_create+0x138/0x500 [ath11k]
+
+Clear the flag once the rings are rebuilt, before ath11k_core_start()
+sends the first HTC message.
+
+Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1
+
+Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+@@ -2264,6 +2264,8 @@ int ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ 		goto err_firmware_stop;
+ 	}
+ 
++	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags);
++
+ 	if (ath11k_frame_mode == ATH11K_HW_TXRX_RAW)
+ 		set_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RAW_MODE, &ab->dev_flags);
+ 
+@@ -2317,8 +2319,6 @@ static int ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ 
+ 	ab->free_vdev_map = (1LL << (ab->num_radios * TARGET_NUM_VDEVS(ab))) - 1;
+ 
+-	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags);
+-
+ 	ret = ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(ab);
+ 	if (ret)
+ 		return ret;
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/459-wifi-ath11k-hold-back-WMI-commands-while-the-firmware-restarts.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/459-wifi-ath11k-hold-back-WMI-commands-while-the-firmware-restarts.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d263f1293fa47e44af12c91ae8375c23d8033517
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/459-wifi-ath11k-hold-back-WMI-commands-while-the-firmware-restarts.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:01:53 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: hold back WMI commands while the firmware restarts
+
+ath11k_core_restart() brings the firmware up outside mac80211's restart,
+so cfg80211 operations keep sending WMI commands while the HTC services
+reconnect and before the firmware reports ready. These commands crash
+the restarting firmware again, and recovery then fails on the unified
+ready timeout:
+
+  ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to receive wmi unified ready event: -110
+  ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to reconfigure driver on crash recovery
+
+With iw setting the RTS threshold in a loop from the moment the firmware
+stops, the firmware crashed 15, 15 and 11 times on three triggers
+before recovery succeeded. With this patch it crashed once per trigger
+(5 of 5).
+
+Return -ESHUTDOWN for commands from outside the restart worker while
+ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY is set. mac80211 replays the configuration when the
+driver restarts the hardware.
+
+Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1
+
+Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+@@ -312,6 +312,10 @@ int ath11k_wmi_cmd_send(struct ath11k_pdev_wmi *wmi, struct sk_buff *skb,
+ 
+ 	might_sleep();
+ 
++	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags) &&
++	    current_work() != &ab->restart_work)
++		return -ESHUTDOWN;
++
+ 	if (ab->hw_params.credit_flow) {
+ 		wait_event_timeout(wmi_ab->tx_credits_wq, ({
+ 			ret = ath11k_wmi_cmd_send_nowait(wmi, skb, cmd_id);
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/460-wifi-ath11k-don-t-disable-ext-IRQs-twice.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/460-wifi-ath11k-don-t-disable-ext-IRQs-twice.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b199ab5a373893d32d6ec411b07dc136370567e1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/460-wifi-ath11k-don-t-disable-ext-IRQs-twice.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+From: Florian Maurer <fmaurer@disroot.org>
+Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:14:46 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: don't disable ext IRQs twice
+
+ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() disables the IRQs at the start of
+every firmware recovery and ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready() enables
+them again at its end. If a recovery fails, they stay disabled. The
+next recovery disables them again, so the disable depth of the ext
+IRQs goes to two and the single enable_irq() leaves them masked. The
+DP rings would then not be serviced after an otherwise successful
+recovery.
+
+This is the same kind of imbalance as the one fixed for suspend/resume
+by commit e56c9d429ba0 ("wifi: ath11k: fix unbalanced IRQ enable/disable
+during suspend/resume"), but caused by a failed recovery.
+
+NAPI already handles this: it is only disabled if it is enabled. The
+ext IRQs are only enabled together with NAPI, so only disable them if
+NAPI is enabled as well. The pcic ext IRQ code has the same pattern, so
+change it there too. The PCI CE IRQs (ath11k_pcic_ce_irqs_disable())
+can have the same imbalance after a failed recovery; they are not
+changed here. The AHB CE IRQs are not affected, as they are enabled
+and disabled through register bits without a disable depth.
+
+On IPQ8074 (AHB) this shows up when a failed recovery (forced with a
+test patch) is followed by another firmware crash: the recovery reports
+success, but TX completions stop, TX fails with "failed to transmit
+frame -12" and the firmware asserts again repeatedly. With this change
+the same sequence recovered 3 out of 3 times. The pcic change is
+compile-tested only.
+
+Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1
+
+Fixes: f7a74e131d3f ("wifi: ath11k: disable interrupts during firmware crash recovery")
+
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+index 3a7b59c..c4ad631 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+@@ -235,9 +235,9 @@ static void __ath11k_ahb_ext_irq_disable(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ 	for (i = 0; i < ATH11K_EXT_IRQ_GRP_NUM_MAX; i++) {
+ 		struct ath11k_ext_irq_grp *irq_grp = &ab->ext_irq_grp[i];
+ 
+-		ath11k_ahb_ext_grp_disable(irq_grp);
+-
++		/* The IRQs are only enabled together with NAPI */
+ 		if (irq_grp->napi_enabled) {
++			ath11k_ahb_ext_grp_disable(irq_grp);
+ 			napi_synchronize(&irq_grp->napi);
+ 			napi_disable(&irq_grp->napi);
+ 			irq_grp->napi_enabled = false;
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c
+index fc6e7da..8cc3018 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pcic.c
+@@ -456,9 +456,9 @@ static void __ath11k_pcic_ext_irq_disable(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ 	for (i = 0; i < ATH11K_EXT_IRQ_GRP_NUM_MAX; i++) {
+ 		struct ath11k_ext_irq_grp *irq_grp = &ab->ext_irq_grp[i];
+ 
+-		ath11k_pcic_ext_grp_disable(irq_grp);
+-
++		/* The IRQs are only enabled together with NAPI */
+ 		if (irq_grp->napi_enabled) {
++			ath11k_pcic_ext_grp_disable(irq_grp);
+ 			napi_synchronize(&irq_grp->napi);
+ 			napi_disable(&irq_grp->napi);
+ 			irq_grp->napi_enabled = false;
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/461-wifi-ath11k-ahb-stop-TX-before-WCSS-is-reset-on-a-firmware-crash.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/461-wifi-ath11k-ahb-stop-TX-before-WCSS-is-reset-on-a-firmware-crash.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ddbdab1a06e8d5637edea09b540dc6ddb1811dc7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/461-wifi-ath11k-ahb-stop-TX-before-WCSS-is-reset-on-a-firmware-crash.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,217 @@
+From: Florian Maurer <fmaurer@disroot.org>
+Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:14:55 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: ahb: stop TX before WCSS is reset on a firmware
+ crash
+
+On IPQ8074 a firmware crash is handled by remoteproc, which stops the
+remote processor and thereby resets WCSS. ath11k sets
+ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, which stops the TX paths, only when it handles
+the QMI server exit event. That event results from the glink teardown
+in rproc_stop() and is handled asynchronously, so it can be processed
+after WCSS is already in reset. A TX in that window writes a ring head
+pointer to the reset block, which ends in an asynchronous SError:
+
+  remoteproc remoteproc0: stopped remote processor cd00000.q6v5_wcss
+  SError Interrupt on CPU3, code 0x00000000bf000002 -- SError
+  pc : ath11k_dp_tx+0x45c/0x878 [ath11k]
+  Kernel panic - not syncing: Asynchronous SError Interrupt
+
+remoteproc sends a QCOM_SSR_BEFORE_SHUTDOWN notification with crashed
+set before it stops the processor. Register for it, like ath10k does on
+SNOC, set ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH there and wait with synchronize_rcu()
+for TX paths which have not seen the flag yet. ath11k_dp_tx() is called
+by mac80211 within RCU read-side critical sections or with BHs
+disabled. Check the flag in ath11k_ce_send() again under ce_lock, so
+that this also covers WMI and HTC.
+
+This stops new TX descriptors, for data and for everything sent through
+CE. Ring pointer updates from the RX and TX completion paths (NAPI, CE
+tasklets) are not stopped by this.
+
+A crash during the restart work of an earlier crash, after the QMI
+firmware start and before ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready() clears
+ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH after ath11k_dp_alloc(), is not covered yet:
+the flag set by the notifier is cleared again, and CE/HTC sends from
+the restart work can still reach the reset WCSS. mac80211 data queues
+are still stopped at that point. That window is a few milliseconds and
+will be addressed separately.
+
+The SSR subsystem name depends on the remoteproc driver, so add it to
+hw_params. Only IPQ8074 sets it for now. qcom_register_ssr_notifier()
+must be reachable from ath11k_ahb, so add the same Kconfig dependency
+on QCOM_RPROC_COMMON as ath10k SNOC has.
+
+Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1
+
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/Kconfig b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/Kconfig
+index 5ab135e..547f875 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/Kconfig
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/Kconfig
+@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ config ATH11K_AHB
+ 	depends on m
+ 	depends on ATH11K
+ 	depends on REMOTEPROC
++	depends on QCOM_RPROC_COMMON || QCOM_RPROC_COMMON=n
+ 	help
+ 	  This module adds support for AHB bus
+ 
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+index c4ad631..2c907f5 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
+ #include "pcic.h"
+ #include <linux/soc/qcom/smem.h>
+ #include <linux/soc/qcom/smem_state.h>
++#include <linux/remoteproc/qcom_rproc.h>
+ 
+ static const struct of_device_id ath11k_ahb_of_match[] = {
+ 	/* TODO: Should we change the compatible string to something similar
+@@ -801,6 +802,60 @@ static const struct ath11k_hif_ops ath11k_ahb_hif_ops_wcn6750 = {
+ 	.ce_irq_disable = ath11k_pci_disable_ce_irqs_except_wake_irq,
+ };
+ 
++static int ath11k_ahb_ssr_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
++				   unsigned long action, void *data)
++{
++	struct ath11k_ahb *ab_ahb = container_of(nb, struct ath11k_ahb, ssr_nb);
++	struct ath11k_base *ab = container_of((void *)ab_ahb, struct ath11k_base,
++					      drv_priv);
++	struct qcom_ssr_notify_data *notify = data;
++
++	if (action != QCOM_SSR_BEFORE_SHUTDOWN || !notify->crashed)
++		return NOTIFY_DONE;
++
++	/* WCSS can be reset before the QMI server exit event sets the flag.
++	 * ath11k_dp_tx() runs in RCU read-side sections or with BHs disabled
++	 * and ath11k_ce_send() checks the flag under ce_lock, so after
++	 * synchronize_rcu() no new TX descriptors are queued.
++	 */
++	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_AHB, "firmware crashed, stopping tx\n");
++	set_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags);
++	synchronize_rcu();
++
++	return NOTIFY_OK;
++}
++
++static void ath11k_ahb_register_ssr_notifier(struct ath11k_base *ab)
++{
++	struct ath11k_ahb *ab_ahb = ath11k_ahb_priv(ab);
++	void *handle;
++
++	if (!ab->hw_params.ssr_name)
++		return;
++
++	ab_ahb->ssr_nb.notifier_call = ath11k_ahb_ssr_notifier;
++	handle = qcom_register_ssr_notifier(ab->hw_params.ssr_name,
++					    &ab_ahb->ssr_nb);
++	if (IS_ERR(handle)) {
++		ath11k_warn(ab, "failed to register ssr notifier: %ld\n",
++			    PTR_ERR(handle));
++		return;
++	}
++
++	ab_ahb->ssr_handle = handle;
++}
++
++static void ath11k_ahb_unregister_ssr_notifier(struct ath11k_base *ab)
++{
++	struct ath11k_ahb *ab_ahb = ath11k_ahb_priv(ab);
++
++	if (!ab_ahb->ssr_handle)
++		return;
++
++	qcom_unregister_ssr_notifier(ab_ahb->ssr_handle, &ab_ahb->ssr_nb);
++	ab_ahb->ssr_handle = NULL;
++}
++
+ static int ath11k_core_get_rproc(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ {
+ 	struct ath11k_ahb *ab_ahb = ath11k_ahb_priv(ab);
+@@ -1203,6 +1258,8 @@ static int ath11k_ahb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+ 		goto err_ce_free;
+ 	}
+ 
++	ath11k_ahb_register_ssr_notifier(ab);
++
+ 	ret = ath11k_core_init(ab);
+ 	if (ret) {
+ 		ath11k_err(ab, "failed to init core: %d\n", ret);
+@@ -1220,6 +1277,7 @@ static int ath11k_ahb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+ 	return 0;
+ 
+ err_ce_free:
++	ath11k_ahb_unregister_ssr_notifier(ab);
+ 	ath11k_ce_free_pipes(ab);
+ 
+ err_hal_srng_deinit:
+@@ -1261,6 +1319,7 @@ static void ath11k_ahb_free_resources(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+ {
+ 	struct platform_device *pdev = ab->pdev;
+ 
++	ath11k_ahb_unregister_ssr_notifier(ab);
+ 	ath11k_ahb_free_irq(ab);
+ 	ath11k_hal_srng_deinit(ab);
+ 	ath11k_ahb_release_smp2p_handle(ab);
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.h
+index 415ddfd..1ad0cdb 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.h
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.h
+@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@ struct ath11k_base;
+ 
+ struct ath11k_ahb {
+ 	struct rproc *tgt_rproc;
++	struct notifier_block ssr_nb;
++	void *ssr_handle;
+ 	struct {
+ 		struct device *dev;
+ 		struct iommu_domain *iommu_domain;
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
+index a7a1636..7bbd32b 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
+@@ -746,6 +746,12 @@ int ath11k_ce_send(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *skb, u8 pipe_id,
+ 
+ 	spin_lock_bh(&ab->ce.ce_lock);
+ 
++	/* Check again with BHs disabled, see ath11k_ahb_ssr_notifier() */
++	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags)) {
++		ret = -ESHUTDOWN;
++		goto err_ce_unlock;
++	}
++
+ 	write_index = pipe->src_ring->write_index;
+ 	nentries_mask = pipe->src_ring->nentries_mask;
+ 
+@@ -792,6 +798,7 @@ int ath11k_ce_send(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *skb, u8 pipe_id,
+ err_unlock:
+ 	spin_unlock_bh(&srng->lock);
+ 
++err_ce_unlock:
+ 	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->ce.ce_lock);
+ 
+ 	return ret;
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+index c171e52..1abc93a 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@ static const struct ath11k_hw_params ath11k_hw_params[] = {
+ 		.coldboot_cal_mm = true,
+ 		.coldboot_cal_ftm = true,
+ 		.cbcal_restart_fw = true,
++		.ssr_name = "q6wcss",
+ 		.fw_mem_mode = 0,
+ 		.num_vdevs = 16 + 1,
+ 		.num_peers = 512,
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.h
+index 52d9f4c..226f4fa 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.h
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.h
+@@ -190,6 +190,7 @@ struct ath11k_hw_params {
+ 	bool coldboot_cal_mm;
+ 	bool coldboot_cal_ftm;
+ 	bool cbcal_restart_fw;
++	const char *ssr_name;
+ 	int fw_mem_mode;
+ 	u32 num_vdevs;
+ 	u32 num_peers;
